                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1][b]Plox Neon\t\t* 8/10[/b][/h1]\nQix? Better, way better and more challenging, of course. Colored and bright, with cool effects but at the same time that 80s retro look with an awesome 80s soundtrack.\n\n[h1][i]INTRO & GAMEPLAY. What is Plox Neon about and how does it work?[/i][/h1]\nPlox Neon is based on classic Qix (or the more recent kbounce for linux users), there's a square field, you move your ball and leave a trail that forms a wall, once you close a portion of field you phisically remove it. Purpose is to remove an amount of field (indicated on top of minimal hud). Sounds ridiculously easy. But while qix had a shapeshifting line bouncing around the field and kbounc hace balls now you have cells and variables. Starts easy but gets more difficult as they grow esponentially in numbers, there are variables that split, or run and bounce around very fast and that gives the player a lot of challenge.\n\n[h1][i]GRAPHIC. Engine And Artistic aspects.[/i][/h1]\nGraphic is simple but clean and very striking because of its strong colors, simple but good looking effects for your trail and removed fields, not to mention the 80s style menus. \n\n[h1][i]SOUNDTRACK. Themes and Accompaniments.[/i][/h1]\n80s retro new wave. Nuff said. I love the 80s and I love music from those years, hence I just love the electronic 80s retro music that pumps out loud through the different maps. Developer should definitely put out a soundtrack pack in the steam store for people like me since this is one of the most endearing aspects of the game (and if they don't hold the rights for that manouvre they should definitely negotiate)\n\n[h1][i]LAST NOTES. What doesn't work?[/i][/h1]\nSimple, entertaining, challenging as it gets more difficult resembling a bullet hell game but the scheme is always the same and maybe the retro style (especially music) may not be appealing to those who not love the 80s like I do. I can't see it as a bad aspect, but if you don't enjoy the atmosphere and the music you will hardly enjoy the game (unless you mute music and launch a Youtube playlist or your own vlc playlist XD).\nAbout gameplay, maybe the small ball you control is a bit too sensible when colliding on other enemies... Because even getting close to them gives death.\n\n[h1][i]TL;DR. Pros And Cons[/i][/h1]\n[h1]+++PROs+++[/h1][list]\n[*][b] CHALLENGING.[/b] It's fun, and gets more and more difficult. It can entertain with almost 100 maps and different kinds and combinations of enemies.\n[*][b] 80s' CHARM.[/b] The game's style and most importantly the music are another strong point for the game. Love the 80s? Get the game and have fun!\n[/list]\n[h1]---CONs---[/h1][list]\n[*][b] 80s' CHARM.[/b] The game relies most of its charm on the 80s' style. Though if you don't enjoy its music, nobody forbids you from turning it off and play your own on vlc or youtube.\n[/list]\n\n[i]I played this game on this machine:\nLaptop Lenovo Z50\nIntel Core i5-4210U\n8Gb RAM DDR3\nGeForce 840M/Intel HD Graphics 4400\nWindows 10 Home x64[/i]\n\n[quote] This review was submitted for [url=http://steamcommunity.com/groups/gaming_until_end]Gaming Until End[/url], through the generous contribution of [url=http://steamcommunity.com/id/HellCowON]HellCow.[/url] [/quote]",
